  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the antisemitic propaganda scene",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the overall antisemitic propaganda scene, which includes the visual material of Sigmund Freud and the textual material questioning the presence of 'Russians'. The rhetorical question 'do you see them often? are they in the room with us now?' implicitly addresses the viewer ('you'), inviting them to participate in the antisemitic trope by questioning the presence of Jews. The user is thus projected onto the scene as the one who is supposed to 'see' or 'notice' the absence of 'Russians' (Jews), making them an active participant in the hateful narrative.",
